.TH COASTLINE 1 "@COASTLINE_MAN_DATE@" "Coastline @CMAKE_PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
coastline \- play Top Gear Rally and Boss Rally
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coastline
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command " [" arguments ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Coastline combines Top Gear Rally and Boss Rally in a stand-alone SDL game.
Game assets must be imported from a Boss Rally disc image and at least one
supported Top Gear Rally ROM image.
Without usable assets, builds with interactive setup open the import wizard.
Incompatible assets require reimporting.
.PP
Command-line overrides apply for the current run.
Matching Options entries are disabled while an override controls them.
Unique prefixes are accepted for choice values; ambiguous prefixes are rejected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-data-dir " DIRECTORY"
Use DIRECTORY for imported assets and saved data instead of system or user
asset roots.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " INI"
Read and save settings in INI instead of the default configuration file.
Data, state, and cache paths are unaffected.
.TP
.BI \-\-asset-pack " PACK"
Select default, boss for Pure PC textures, or an installed mod pack.
Optional packs override files from the default and selected regional packs.
.TP
.BI \-\-language " LANGUAGE"
Select imported text and fonts, such as en-us, en-gb, or ja.
.TP
.BI \-\-region " REGION"
Select usa, eur, or jpn models and images independently of language.
.TP
.BI \-\-width " PIXELS"
Set the window width, from 1 to 16384 pixels.
.TP
.BI \-\-height " PIXELS"
Set the window height, from 1 to 16384 pixels.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Cover the display.
.TP
.B \-\-windowed
Start in a window.
.TP
.BI \-\-antialias " SAMPLES"
Select 1, 2, 4, or 8 samples per pixel.
A value of 1 disables multisample anti-aliasing.
.TP
.B \-\-no-vsync
Present frames without waiting for vertical synchronisation.
.TP
.BI \-\-aspect-ratio " RATIO"
Use auto to fill the output, a ratio such as 4:3 or 21:9,
or a positive finite width-to-height number such as 1.6.
Explicit ratios add bars where necessary.
.TP
.BI \-\-gpu-preset " PRESET"
Select n64, br, ultra, worst, or low-power.
N64 selects a 320x240 internal base, 4:3, and Consumer CRT.
BR selects a 640x480 internal base, 4:3, Pure PC textures, PC CRT,
and PC CD music.
An explicit aspect ratio can expand either base resolution.
Ultra selects maximum graphics quality and full screen.
Worst selects minimum quality without filters and preserves the aspect ratio.
Low-power requests a lower-power GPU with moderate graphics settings.
Other explicit graphics arguments override the preset.
.TP
.BI \-\-gpu " PREFERENCE"
Select auto, high-performance, or low-power.
SDL selects an available adapter matching the preference when possible.
.TP
.B \-\-debug-gpu
Enable GPU validation when the backend provides validation layers.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.B \-\-minimized
Start with the window minimised.
Available in debug builds only.
.if @COASTLINE_MAN_SETUP@ \{\
.TP
.B \-\-reset
Remove generated asset packs and asset caches, preserving settings, saves,
decals, and custom packs, then start the game or setup.
Confirm with y or n at the terminal, without case sensitivity.
.TP
.B \-\-factory-reset
Delete all configuration, data, state, and cache, including saves, decals,
custom packs, and an explicit INI file, then start the game or setup.
Confirmation is required.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes-really
Confirm either reset without prompting.
.\}
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B import
Convert disc and ROM assets.
See
.BR coastline-import (1).
.TP
.B import-pak
Import Controller Pak notes.
See
.BR coastline-import-pak (1).
.TP
.BI "export-pak " "[\-\-release REGION] FILE"
Export saved notes to a Controller Pak image.
REGION is usa, eur, or jpn and defaults to usa.
For an existing four-pak image, replace the first pak and preserve the other
three.
.TP
.B run-script
Run scripted input and screenshots.
See
.BR coastline-run-script (1).
.SH CONTROLS
Alt+Enter or F11 toggles full screen.
F cycles through legacy FPS, full statistics, and no overlay.
Legacy FPS uses game resolution and filters.
Full statistics use output resolution and OS display scaling.
Ctrl+U toggles unlocked frame pacing.
V changes vertical synchronisation outside screens that accept text.
.SH FILES
On Linux and BSD, the XDG base directories apply, each with a coastline
subdirectory.
Defaults are ~/.config/coastline, ~/.local/share/coastline,
~/.local/state/coastline, and ~/.cache/coastline.
macOS and Windows use platform-specific application directories.
.PP
BossRally.ini stores settings.
The data directory includes assets and Controller Pak notes.
game.log is written in the state directory.
.PP
On Linux, GameMode=1 under [Game] in BossRally.ini requests Feral GameMode at
startup when its client library and service are available.
The default is 1; set GameMode=0 to disable the request.
The request ends on exit and persists across internal game restarts.
Missing clients and failed requests do not prevent play.
Other platforms ignore the setting.
Import and Controller Pak commands do not request GameMode.
.PP
System assets are searched before user assets, including the installation's
share/coastline and /usr/share/coastline on Unix systems.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME
Override corresponding Unix base directories.
Relative values are ignored.
.TP
.B SDL_LOGGING
Set SDL log levels unless \-\-debug overrides them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success or a normal exit.
A nonzero status indicates invalid arguments, an import failure, or a startup
error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coastline-import (1),
.BR coastline-import-pak (1),
.BR coastline-run-script (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/Tatsh/coastline/issues.
